k Turks, from Seljuk raids into Armenia in the mid-11th century to the end of the…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/norman-conquest"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/norman-conquest.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Norman Conquest</span><span class="enc-type">War · 1066</span><span class="enc-snip">The Norman Conquest was the invasion and occupation of England by William, Duke of Normandy, in 1066 and the following years.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/song-dai-viet-war"><span class="enc-name">Song–Đại Việt war</span><span class="enc-type">War · 1075–1077</span><span class="enc-snip">The Song–Đại Việt war was fought between the Song dynasty of China and the Lý dynasty of Đại Việt in 1075–1077.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/first-crusade"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/first-crusade.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">First Crusade</span><span class="enc-type">Campaign · captured Jerusalem 1099</span><span class="enc-snip">The First Crusade was a military expedition by western European Christians that captured Jerusalem in 1099 and established the Crusader states.</span></a></li></ul></section>
